Flecha: flechaPrivate.createTab loads the page once it is a tab.

createTab (patch 0034) made the WebContents, started the load and only then
put it in the tab strip. A page of the browser is built inside LoadURL(), and
chrome://settings asks for the tab's autofill client there
(SettingsUI::SettingsUI, ContentAutofillClient::FromWebContents), which a
WebContents only gets with its tab helpers, on becoming a tab. So opening
Settings in a Space with separate cookies and logins (Edit Profile, say,
which the shell reopened in the Space's partition) crashed the browser.

The tab is added first and loads after, the order Chromium's own
Navigate() keeps (the tab model, then the load).

--- a/chrome/browser/extensions/api/flecha_private/flecha_private_api.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/extensions/api/flecha_private/flecha_private_api.cc
@@ -758,13 +758,17 @@
   std::unique_ptr<content::WebContents> contents =
       content::WebContents::Create(create_params);
   content::WebContents* raw = contents.get();
-  contents->GetController().LoadURL(url, content::Referrer(),
-                                    ui::PAGE_TRANSITION_AUTO_TOPLEVEL,
-                                    std::string());
+  // Flecha: into the tab strip first, then the load. Being a tab is what
+  // gives the contents its tab helpers, and a WebUI page is made inside
+  // LoadURL() and may need them there: chrome://settings asks for the
+  // autofill client, which crashed the browser when it wasn't a tab yet.
   host->GetBrowserWindowInterface()->GetTabStripModel()->AddWebContents(
       std::move(contents), TabStripModel::kNoTab,
       ui::PAGE_TRANSITION_AUTO_TOPLEVEL,
       active ? AddTabTypes::ADD_ACTIVE : AddTabTypes::ADD_NONE);
+  raw->GetController().LoadURL(url, content::Referrer(),
+                               ui::PAGE_TRANSITION_AUTO_TOPLEVEL,
+                               std::string());
   return RespondNow(WithArguments(ExtensionTabUtil::GetTabId(raw)));
 }
 
